{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For a stone</b> that destroyed cities and towns and built Babylon — for the stone will testify that it was built from violence." "<b>And a beam</b>: the hard place in the wood of the beams, and it is called qeshar in the foreign tongue; therefore after it: 'Woe to him who builds a city.'"], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The lemma וכפיס appears in some Hebrew Bible editions as וכפיס from Habakkuk 2:11; the term denotes a structural wooden element. לעז rendered as 'the foreign tongue,' standard in Ibn Ezra for Old French or vernacular."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:11.192107339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}